@h3 ref2va 16:9 lite
style: live-action, cinematic surreal body horror, photorealistic
$host = __bh_host__
$inner = __bh_inner__
$room = __bh_room__
$seam = {down the centerline from the sternum to the navel|down the length of the spine|from the crown of the head down the middle of the face}

CAST
HOST (image 1): $host
INNER: $inner

SHOT 10s | push in, slow
HOST stands alone in $room, framed from the knees up, slightly tense but otherwise normal. A clean, deliberate seam appears $seam, as though the body were a garment built around something inside it. The seam slowly opens and, without blood or injury, the outer body separates like a fitted soft suit, skin and clothing pulling apart together as one hollow shell. From within, INNER steps forward in one controlled movement, lifting one leg free and then the other. The empty shell stays upright for a moment like a shed skin, then folds softly to the floor. In the final moment INNER turns toward the camera with a composed, unreadable expression.
SFX: quiet room ambience; a soft fabric-like separation; slow deliberate footsteps; the gentle collapse of the empty shell
MUSIC: N/A
